    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let the weight of one canoe be denoted by \\( C \\) and the weight of one bowling ball by \\( B \\). According to the problem, seven bowling balls weigh the same as three canoes. This relationship can be expressed mathematically as:\n\n\\[ 7B = 3C \\]\n\nWe are also given that two canoes weigh a total of 56 pounds. This can be written as:\n\n\\[ 2C = 56 \\]\n\nFrom the second equation, we can solve for \\( C \\):\n\n\\[ C = \\frac{56}{2} = 28 \\]\n\nNow that we know the weight of one canoe is 28 pounds, we can substitute \\( C = 28 \\) into the first equation to find the weight of one bowling ball \\( B \\):\n\n\\[ 7B = 3C \\]\n\\[ 7B = 3 \\times 28 \\]\n\\[ 7B = 84 \\]\n\\[ B = \\frac{84}{7} = 12 \\]\n\nTherefore, the weight of one bowling ball is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) pounds.",
